From 5bd129e3d3ee975ef85794fd021d90d026998a88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OOS <oos@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] JSC: support eager WebAssembly BBQ compilation

OOS favors steady-state application performance over startup latency. Add an
opt-in mode that compiles and installs every WebAssembly function with BBQ
before module instantiation completes. Compilation failures reject the module
instead of silently falling back to the interpreter.

Honor useWasmOSR while generating BBQ code. This avoids building an unused
loop entrypoint when eager BBQ compilation and interpreter-free execution make
IPInt-to-BBQ loop OSR unnecessary.
